-- Spanish 2 course record. Safe to run more than once.
alter table public.courses add column if not exists video_url text;

insert into public.courses (slug, title, subject, credits, focus)
values ('spanish-2', 'Spanish 2', 'Electives', 1.0, $j$Spanish 2 is a one credit world language course that builds on Spanish 1 and helps students speak, read, write and understand Spanish with growing confidence while learning to love and serve neighbors of every nation. Students review the present tense, study reflexive verbs and the daily routine, irregular verbs, saber and conocer and the personal a, the preterite and imperfect past tenses, direct and indirect object pronouns, verbs like gustar, comparisons, por and para, formal and informal commands, travel and directions, health and emergency vocabulary, the present progressive, the future tense, careers and technology, holidays and traditions, retelling Bible stories, prayer, testimony and hospitality, letters and emails, and honest interpreting and service. Each lesson connects to Scripture in the King James Version, and all Scripture quotations in the course are in the King James Version. The course includes six units, lesson checks, unit quizzes, assessments, discussions and a final portfolio and exam. Students practice reading, writing, listening and speaking, and learn about the cultures of Spanish speaking peoples with respect.$j$)
on conflict (slug) do nothing;
